ased Syst. 2021;217:106817.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Hamilton, W. L., Ying, Z. &amp; Leskovec, J. Inductive representation learning on large graphs. in <i>NIPS</i> (2017).</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Ostfeld A, Salomons E, Ormsbee L, Uber JG, Bros CM. Battle of the water calibration networks. J. Water Resourc. Plan. Manag. 2012;138:523&#x2013;532.</Citation></Reference></ReferenceList></PubmedData></PubmedArticle><PubmedArticle><MedlineCitation Status="MEDLINE" Owner="NLM" IndexingMethod="Automated"><PMID Version="1">37482904</PMID><DateCompleted><Year>2023</Year><Month>11</Month><Day>27</Day></DateCompleted><DateRevised><Year>2025</Year><Month>09</Month><Day>30</Day></DateRevised><Article PubModel="Print-Electronic"><Journal><ISSN IssnType="Electronic">1097-0134</ISSN><JournalIssue CitedMedium="Internet"><Volume>91</Volume><Issue>12</Issue><PubDate><Year>2023</Year><Month>Dec</Month></PubDate></JournalIssue><Title>Proteins</Title><ISOAbbreviation>Proteins</ISOAbbreviation></Journal><ArticleTitle>VoroIF-GNN: Voronoi tessellation-derived protein-protein interface assessment using a graph neural network.</ArticleTitle><Pagination><StartPage>1879</StartPage><EndPage>1888</EndPage><MedlinePgn>1879-1888</MedlinePgn></Pagination><ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/prot.26554</ELocationID><Abstract><AbstractText>We present VoroIF-GNN (Voronoi InterFace Graph Neural Network), a novel method for assessing inter-subunit interfaces in a structural model of a protein-protein complex, relying solely on the input structure without any additional information. Given a multimeric protein structural model, we derive interface contacts from the Voronoi tessellation of atomic balls, construct a graph of those contacts, and predict the accuracy of every contact using an attention-based GNN. The contact-level predictions are then summarized to produce whole interface-level scores. VoroIF-GNN was blindly tested for its ability to estimate the ac